      "next_deadline": "2026-27 cycle: NOFA published September 2025, CDBG and ESG applications September 25 to December 18, 2025 (extended to January 9, 2026), Board hearing April 28, 2026, adoption July 14, 2026. HOME applications are accepted on a rolling basis until funds are committed (RivcoCDBG@rivco.org, (951) 955-5936). The 2027-28 NOFA is expected in late September 2026 with a mid-December deadline.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "Riverside County's Housing and Workforce Solutions (HWS) department runs the Urban County HUD programs, PLHA, HHAP, Homekey+ sponsorships and project loans, while the Housing Authority of the County of Riverside (HACR, same Board sitting as Commissioners) supplies project-based vouchers, housing successor funds and land; rivcohws.org and harivco.org block automated access, so records were built from Board of Supervisors files on riversidecountyca.iqm2.com and media.rivcocob.org, RUHS Behavioral Health, the Assessor and the County Housing Element. The Urban County covers the unincorporated area and cooperating cities (cooperation agreements for FY 2027-29 approved July 28, 2026); Riverside, Moreno Valley, Corona, Temecula, Palm Springs, Indio and other large cities are separate entitlements (Pass 3). HOME money is small relative to the county's size (about $1.6 million a year for development) and is used as a $1 million to $1.6 million soft loan alongside HACR PBVs and tax credits; CDBG is district-allocated and rarely funds multifamily. Davis-Bacon applies to HOME projects of 12 or more units. Source is the Board file for the 2026-27 One Year Action Plan (attachment 2026-2027 One Year Action Plan, FileOpen ID 88444).",
