      "layering_notes": "Riverside County's Housing and Workforce Solutions (HWS) department runs the Urban County HUD programs, PLHA, HHAP, Homekey+ sponsorships and project loans, while the Housing Authority of the County of Riverside (HACR, same Board sitting as Commissioners) supplies project-based vouchers, housing successor funds and land; rivcohws.org and harivco.org block automated access, so records were built from Board of Supervisors files on riversidecountyca.iqm2.com and media.rivcocob.org, RUHS Behavioral Health, the Assessor and the County Housing Element. PBVs are the County's primary contribution to 4% and 9% deals and nearly every County loan, PLHA commitment, Homekey+ sponsorship and HHAP operating subsidy attaches to a PBV project; developers should treat the annual HACR PBV RFP as the entry point to the County system. Davis-Bacon applies to PBV new construction and rehabilitation of nine or more units. Source is the HUD-50075 Streamlined Annual Plan attached to the March 24, 2026 Board file (Detail_LegiFile.aspx?ID=29959); voucher count from the FY 2025-26 SEMAP CEQA notice (ceqanet 2026071100).",
